  "title": "What's going on with these multiple 'Best Answer' notifications.",
  "content": "<p>Just now:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/02f50509-391b-4161-9d12-c88d41f000f0.png\" /></figure><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/stm32-mcus-products-25/minimum-current-requirement-for-external-vref-on-stm32g474-167348\"></oembed><p>Notifications of 2 different posts marked as ‘Best Answer’ for the same question at, essentially, the same time.</p><p> </p><p>Also had similar earlier this morning:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/8feff44b-2bdf-4471-9cb5-7fd065d304fa.png\" /></figure><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/others-stm32-mcus-related-142/bare-metal-tmc2209-uart-driver-for-stm32-cmsis-feedback-on-api-design-next-steps-167295\"></oembed><p>This time <strong>five</strong> ‘Best’ answers!</p><p> </p><p>What’s going on?!</p><p> </p><p>​<user-mention data-id=\"108703\">@nbsown</user-mention> and ​<user-mention data-id=\"107084\">@Rafo</user-mention> were you, perhaps, trying to mark <em>multiple</em> post all as ‘Best Answer’ ?</p><p>Or did you just change your minds ?</p>",
